---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import "../styles/annotation-ops.css";
import AudienceBadge from "../components/AudienceBadge.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Annotation Operations"
  active="annotation-ops"
  section="architecture"
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Annotation Operations</span>
      <p class="home-hero-audience"><AudienceBadge tier="both" /></p>
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">From paragraph intent to pipeline action.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-lede">
        This lane turns reading decisions into reusable intelligence. Every
        marker and instruction moves through a durable queue, lands in a
        structured chapter file, and becomes available to AI assistants, search,
        and future automation.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section id="s01-path" class="stack">
    <h2><span class="num">01</span> The operating path</h2>
    <div class="ops-flow">
      <div class="ops-node">
        <h3>1) Reader workbench</h3>
        <p>
          Paragraph hover activates the right-hand workspace. Markers and notes
          are captured immediately.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ops-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ops-node">
        <h3>2) Queue ledger</h3>
        <p>
          Action instructions accumulate in a local queue and can be copied as
          one execution set.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ops-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ops-node">
        <h3>3) Durable chapter file</h3>
        <p>
          One click sync writes a chapter-level JSON handoff with markers,
          notes, and the full queue text.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="ops-arrow">→</div>
      <div class="ops-node">
        <h3>4) Pipeline intelligence</h3>
        <p>
          Classification and queued actions feed extraction, verification,
          augmentation, and future auto-marking.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="s02-scopes" class="stack">
    <h2><span class="num">02</span> Three scopes, one queue</h2>
    <div class="grid-3">
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Paragraph</strong>
        <p class="small">
          Fine-grained edits, doctrinal tags, and contextual research tied to
          one location.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Book</strong>
        <p class="small">
          Structural instructions that apply across chapters in the same title.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Global</strong>
        <p class="small">
          Reusable production rules for style, quality checks, and guardrails
          across titles.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <hr />

  <section id="s03-future" class="stack">
    <h2><span class="num">03</span> What this unlocks next</h2>
    <div class="grid-2">
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Auto-marking from learned patterns</strong>
        <p class="small">
          As pattern density grows, the pipeline can pre-label likely esoteric
          or reality sections before author review.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Cross-book retrieval</strong>
        <p class="small">
          Any queued insight can be reused in later books, audits, and
          interactive assistant sessions.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Cost-efficient execution packs</strong>
        <p class="small">
          Batch copy of accumulated instructions reduces repeated prompting and
          keeps work sessions focused.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="card card-tight">
        <strong>Planner-aware auto views</strong>
        <p class="small">
          When annotation lanes expand in the plan, the site snapshot flow can
          detect and create missing architecture views.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
